appl: actor=EditorConfig-aware tooling; action=stop ancestor .editorconfig lookup; trigger=resolving settings for repository files; modality=CONFIGURATION FACT; scope=repository files; exceptions=nested .editorconfig files still apply; timing=settings resolution; enforcement=tool behaviour, not executed; loading=not an instruction file
compared: FG-L1-5d16334fbd FG-L1-7a42211469 FG-L1-750d02a508 FG-L1-e87ce2918c
rationale: .editorconfig:2 'root = true' verified. Same assessment as the identical M/M1/L0 claims: a format-defined lookup marker scoping the registered formatting/style values, with no agent obligation; both Claude runs classified it as IMPLEMENTATION.
scenario: N/A as a constraint: repository values are unchanged by root=false; only unspecified properties from outside the repository could be inherited.
conf: MEDIUM
open_issue: Methodology: revisit with the other five root=true claims if Stage 2 counts configuration-inheritance boundaries as constraints.

@@ CIS-L1-0002
disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: PROCEDURAL INSTRUCTION (working directory for frontend commands)
appl: actor=agent running frontend commands via the frontend.commands facet; action=run frontend workspace commands from the workspace directory frontend/<Name>.Web/; trigger=running install/build/test/lint/audit commands of an existing workspace; modality=MUST (imperative); scope=frontend.commands capability facet; exceptions=the initial scaffold command creates the workspace from the repository root; timing=whenever these commands run; enforcement=instruction only; loading=capability facet read by project-structure, verify, build-fix, development-workflow and security-scan (not always loaded)
compared: FG-L1-2af01b370e FG-L1-124e24d760 FG-L1-a272c571b8 FG-L1-b26abc5d23 FG-L1-6927a2a49d FG-L1-c52d07c934
rationale: commands.md:5 verified. The same line's other sentences are registered (install only through add-dependency FG-L1-2af01b370e; workspace location FG-L1-124e24d760), and the facet's other command imperatives are registered (npm ci FG-L1-c52d07c934, inspect package.json FG-L1-6927a2a49d/FG-L1-b26abc5d23), but no L1 group states the working-directory instruction (grep). By the union's own granularity for this facet it is an unrepresented procedural clause. Its practical weight is low (many violations simply fail); recorded as a proposal, not an EXTRA verdict. Codex NOVEL confirmed as distinct.
scenario: The agent runs 'npm --prefix frontend/<Name>.Web run build' from the repository root: build succeeds, all registered groups hold, the stated working-directory procedure is not followed.
conf: MEDIUM
proposal: MUST (procedural) | running commands of the frontend workspace (frontend.commands facet) | Run the frontend workspace commands from the workspace directory (frontend/<Name>.Web/).
policy_hint: DEP-024 (Codex suggestion; not adjudicated)

