@@ CIS-L1-U0004
disp: EXISTING_GROUP_NEEDS_EXPLICIT_FACET
nature: HOOK_RUNTIME_BEHAVIOR (identity key of the deny-once retry gate)
appl: actor=pre-shell-command PreToolUse dependency gate; action=treat commands as identical after trimming and collapsing every whitespace run to one space, including inside quoted arguments; trigger=retry of a dependency-classified command within the 30-minute grace period; modality=ENFORCEMENT PREDICATE; scope=dependency-changing shell commands in the active root; exceptions=force/reference classifications are handled earlier; timing=PreToolUse; enforcement=static code read (line 185); Codex reports a pure-copy probe, not re-run here; loading=hook code
match: FG-L1-1001431838
compared: FG-L1-1c1d40efd7 FG-L1-bb27864162 FG-L1-a272c571b8
rationale: pre-shell-command.mjs:185-190 verified: key = command.trim().replace(/\s+/g, ' '). FG-L1-1001431838 says the 'identical command' is allowed on retry; the designed key is whitespace-normalised, so a command differing only in whitespace runs (also inside quotes, e.g. a different quoted path) reuses the allowance. Recorded as a precise boundary of the existing gate; it adds no agent obligation (the gate is already registered as an effective reminder in FG-L1-1c1d40efd7).
scenario: 'npm install "./a  b.tgz"' is denied; 'npm install "./a b.tgz"' (a different path) is then allowed because both normalise to the same key.
conf: HIGH
facet: FG-L1-1001431838 | NEW_BEHAVIOR_BOUNDARY | 'Identical' means equal after trimming and collapsing every whitespace run to a single space, including inside quoted arguments; commands that differ only in such whitespace share one retry allowance.

