disp: DISTINCT_UNREPRESENTED_CLAUSE
nature: WORKFLOW REVIEW STEP (production debug/development flags in the configuration layer)
appl: actor=agent running the security-scan workflow; action=review production debug/development flags; trigger=scan covering the secrets and configuration layer; modality=PROCEDURAL (investigation prompt); scope=security-scan workflow via scan-layers.md; exceptions=only applicable surfaces; not an automatic vulnerability declaration; timing=during the scan; enforcement=instruction only; loading=private reference read by security-scan
compared: FG-L1-b8e7f36df1 FG-L1-93a5d935e8 FG-L1-d08af16e1a FG-L1-0839fd096c
rationale: scan-layers.md:19 verified; both runs classified the review list as investigation prompts and no L1 group mentions debug/development flags (grep). The registered neighbours concern surface discovery, fail-safe startup and 'not automatically safe' items. Unrepresented review step, consistent with the other scan-layer proposals.
scenario: A scan verifies secrets and fail-safe configuration but never looks at a production configuration that enables a debug feature flag.
conf: MEDIUM
open_issue: The same line also lists certificate-validation bypasses, credential-bearing URLs, verbose production error configuration and committed .env files; not checked beyond this claim (no extraction).
proposal: PROCEDURAL (review step) | security scan covering the secrets and configuration layer | Review production debug/development flags as part of the secrets and configuration layer of a security scan.
policy_hint: EXC-015 context / WF-020 (non-binding)

@@ CIS-L1-U0015
disp: NOT_AN_INDEPENDENT_CONSTRAINT
nature: TECHNICAL_PREREQUISITE (LogContext needs the enricher)
appl: actor=agent configuring Serilog; action=enable Enrich.FromLogContext; trigger=using LogContext.PushProperty; modality=TECHNICAL FACT ('requires'); scope=logging private reference serilog.md; exceptions=none; timing=configuration; enforcement=library behaviour; loading=private technique reference
compared: FG-L1-d8a716f67f FG-L1-36e12d0f5b
rationale: serilog.md:90 verified: a library prerequisite stated inside a technique bullet; both runs classified it as technique. Same assessment as M1/L0.
scenario: N/A: omitting the enricher is a functional defect of the chosen technique, not a separate rule.
conf: HIGH
